@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### DASHBOARDS-REPORTS: manager dashboard, ticket report and CSV exports
### Log in first (cookie), e.g. POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login with manager@sdp.test / Passw0rd!
### Demo accounts: mia (Service Desk manager), ian (Infrastructure manager), admin, assets, tech (Theo), nia (Infrastructure tech)

### manager dashboard: SLA, workload, CSAT, trend. ?days = 7, 30 (default), 90 or all
GET {{baseUrl}}/manager-api/dashboard

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/manager-api/dashboard?days=7

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/manager-api/dashboard?days=all

### admin only: one team (an IT_SUPPORT department id from GET /admin-api/departments?kind=IT_SUPPORT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/manager-api/dashboard?department=PASTE_DEPARTMENT_ID

### negative: invalid period -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/manager-api/dashboard?days=14

### negative: as admin, a BUSINESS department or a malformed id -> 400 (as a manager the param is ignored: 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/manager-api/dashboard?department=nope

### negative: as an employee, technician or asset manager -> 403; with no cookie -> 401

### admin overview (same numbers for all teams) under "overview", old keys unchanged
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin-api/dashboard?days=30

### negative: -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin-api/dashboard?days=abc

### technician dashboard (log in as tech@sdp.test): own tickets, SLA, CSAT, time logged
GET {{baseUrl}}/tech-api/dashboard?days=30

### negative: -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/tech-api/dashboard?days=0

### asset statistics (assets@sdp.test or admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/stats

### ticket report preview, same filters as the CSV. from/to are IST dates (YYYY-MM-DD), to is inclusive
GET {{baseUrl}}/report-api/tickets?status=CLOSED&priority=HIGH&from=2026-09-01&to=2026-10-03&page=1&limit=15

### CSV download (UTF-8 with BOM, CRLF). Headers: X-Row-Count, X-Truncated
GET {{baseUrl}}/report-api/tickets.csv?from=2026-09-01&to=2026-10-03

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/report-api/tickets.csv?q=printer

### negative: impossible date, wrong format, or from after to -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/report-api/tickets.csv?from=2026-02-31

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/report-api/tickets.csv?from=03-10-2026

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/report-api/tickets.csv?from=2026-10-03&to=2026-10-01

### an unknown status or priority is not an error (same as the ticket list): 200 with just the header row
GET {{baseUrl}}/report-api/tickets.csv?status=DONE

### negative: a manager passing department of another team is ignored (their own team is always used); an employee -> 403

### asset CSV (assets@sdp.test or admin); ?status=IN_STOCK etc
GET {{baseUrl}}/report-api/assets.csv

### negative: unknown status -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/report-api/assets.csv?status=LOST

### negative: a manager or technician -> 403
